las vegas reps say the city was duped  when a public pool was rented out it's a  story the i-team first broke after a  pool party  resulted in a shooting now the i-team  has obtained the documents at the center  of the controversy vanessa murphy here  live in studio with an update brian city  reps say the person who rented out the  pool claimed it was for a family reunion  the i-team learned it was actually an  advertised party with tickets to  purchase for admission  and there was also a cash prize for the  best twerker  metro police say the party resulted in  at least one person  opening fire so here are the documents  we obtained  a request to rent out a public pool on  the sunday of memorial day weekend  for a family slash friends reunion with  100 to 150 expected  and a permit issued to rent the pavilion  center pool in summerlin from  3 to 9 p.m for 960 dollars  metro police say just before 9 at night  more than  100 rounds were fired no serious  injuries were reported and metro  along with the atf are working to  identify  people involved the i-team talked with  councilwoman victoria seaman a couple of  days later  she said the city was investigating what  happened on its end  and pool rentals are suspended metro is  asking  anyone with information to contact the  gang unit  or to leave a tip through crime stoppers  that number  is 702-385-5555  the name of the person who rented out  the pool is redacted on the documents  the i-team obtained  however i tracked down the party  organizer on instagram  he would not provide his full name but  he provided  a statement he claims he never filled  out that request  to rent out the pool for a family  reunion he says he deeply apologizes he  is not a gang member of any kind  and he does not plan on throwing any  events  anytime soon we'll put that full  statement at eight newsnow dot com
 

